  "label": "Historical context of lynching in the United States",
  "description": "The statistic of 3,446 Black people killed by the KKK over 86 years refers to lynching, a form of extrajudicial punishment and racial terror. Understanding the historical context of lynching — its prevalence, its purpose, and its impact on Black communities — requires external knowledge of U.S. racial history and the history of racial violence.",
